Changes made for this fork:
- Added dashboard/plugin_api.py and the wolfmark_ledger/ package: a read-only backend
  over Hermes' session_model_usage and sessions tables, with provider-aware
  pricing and no cross-provider rate borrowing.
- Added a plugin-owned timestamped call store (wolfmark_ledger/store.py) and
  observer-only collector (wolfmark_ledger/collector.py) using Hermes'
  post_api_request, post_auxiliary_call and api_request_error hooks. It records
  accounting metadata only: no prompts, responses, credentials or telemetry.
- Added a separately labelled cumulative baseline and reconciliation against
  state.db growth; period figures come only from timestamped call rows.
- Added per-call context-tier pricing for timestamped rows and an explicitly
  labelled average-prompt estimate for the cumulative baseline.
- Added dashboard/manifest.json and backend attribution in plugin.yaml.
- Added the "All Hermes" view to desktop/plugin.js; the live chip and
  focused-session pane are retained from upstream.
- Added catalogue/rates.json and scripts/gen-catalogue.py.
- Added Python unit tests, collector/period tests and backend reconciliation tests.
- Added interactive, theme-aware SVG analytics, a sortable Model Explorer,
  read-only timestamped chart aggregation, strict per-call cache economics,
  exact shared filters and pricing/cache coverage disclosures.
- Added isolated analytics tests and a development-only browser review harness;
  no external charting service or runtime chart dependency is required.

Spend Sense development baseline: WolfMark Cost Ledger 0.5.0 acceptance
candidate, including subsequently reviewed Desktop UI and regression changes.
The earlier 0.2.4-ui-1 release is retained privately as a behavioural reference.
Historical development commits and operational data are not part of this tree.

